{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1299070-plague-doctor-mage-during-the-black-death-which-hermetic-house","id":1299070,"title":"Plague Doctor Mage during the Black Death; which Hermetic House?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-23T16:22:24-07:00","id":1299070,"title":"Plague Doctor Mage during the Black Death; which Hermetic House?","content":"One of my players had a concept for an NPC who is a really unstable thaumivore who can only exist in his Sanctum, with brief forays into areas with no sleepers and loose consensus.<br /> <br /> He was infected with the bubonic plague during the great Black Death outbreak which spread across Europe in the 1350s. He only survived through a minor miracle; an Entropy/Life/Time effect turned him into a sort of lich. He is not alive or dead, but stuck in the process of dying, and the spell that keeps him alive (granting him the Immortality Merit) requires infusions of Tass and Quintessence. His special &quot;doom&quot; is to be cured of the pathogen infecting him; ironically it is only the presence of this virulent disease that keeps him alive!<br /> <br /> He wears full plague doctor garb to hide his hideous deformity from the plague, and to keep others safe from his infection. He burns incense in the beak of the mask to shield his own senses from the smell of putrefaction, and as a ritual focus.<br /> <br /> Mages come to him when they are in desperate need of help; his reputation is terrible. Demons keep him alive. Either that, or he's a Vampire of some kind. No, no, he's a Wraith that has clung onto its body for 100s of years. But people know that his understanding of necrosis, tissue and infection are unparalleled, along with his mastery of the Life, Entropy and Prime Spheres. Furthermore, he is in a tiny minority of ancient Mages who weren't wiped away during the Avatar Storm; since he never developed the Spirit sphere beyond the 2nd level, he never moved to a Horizon Realm, and he was shielded from the events of the late 90s. That means he may even be the oldest and most powerful Hermetic Mage in existence... if a rather odd one.<br /> <br /> So, which of the founding Houses fits him best? I've ruled out Tremere, and from what I can see none of the others really fit :-(","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T18:29:03-07:00","id":1299090,"title":"","content":"House Bonisagus would be my suggestion. It seems to fit his scholarly nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T02:10:58-07:00","id":1299152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1299070-plague-doctor-mage-during-the-black-death-which-hermetic-house?p=1299090#post1299090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">House Bonisagus would be my suggestion. It seems to fit his scholarly nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice! I overlooked them because the description didn't mention Life, but honestly the setup seems to fit a medieval physician very well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T07:30:42-07:00","id":1299203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1299070-plague-doctor-mage-during-the-black-death-which-hermetic-house?p=1299152#post1299152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nice! I overlooked them because the description didn't mention Life, but honestly the setup seems to fit a medieval physician very well.</div> </div> </div> </div>While they're probably best known for their work in magical metaphysics and the like (Prime, Countermagic, and related areas), they will study anything and everything that can expand the frontiers and boundaries of the Art of Magic (including things like immortality, necromancy, and other oddities). They also work to maintain and strengthen the Order as a whole, so his unique status after the Avatar Storm makes him a potential pivotal part of shepherding the Hermetics through that period.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T07:52:12-07:00","id":1299212,"title":"","content":"I'd agree Bonisagus is a fairly safe option, though you could have him be a former Cosian. If he doesn't shift his paradigm, by the modern era he'd be much closer to a Hermetic than a Progenitor. That would also give you a reason for his bad rep, the guy knows a huge amount of Hermetic lore but he's related to the forerunners of the Technocracy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T09:15:45-07:00","id":1299233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1299070-plague-doctor-mage-during-the-black-death-which-hermetic-house?p=1299203#post1299203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While they're probably best known for their work in magical metaphysics and the like (Prime, Countermagic, and related areas), they will study anything and everything that can expand the frontiers and boundaries of the Art of Magic (including things like immortality, necromancy, and other oddities). They also work to maintain and strengthen the Order as a whole, so his unique status after the Avatar Storm makes him a potential pivotal part of shepherding the Hermetics through that period.</div> </div> </div> </div>It'd be interesting to have certain Traditions figures showing up trying to pressure him into taking a more active role in the new Council, &quot;you're the only Hermetic from that period who is left alive, it would appease traditionalists and hard-liners&quot; etc. but him always turning them down, arguing that it's ridiculous to argue that power and age make someone a good ruler.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}